nodecode-distro-reader is a rewrite of Distro-Media's Distro-Media/hermes-plugin-distro-reader:

  https://github.com/Distro-Media/hermes-plugin-distro-reader
  commit 57bfa385e6dd9e1dc1d5230d0907c1c07d248ae7
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Distro Media (LICENSE)

The plugin was a portable Agent Plugins v1 package: a plugin.json declaring Distro's
hosted reader an untrusted MCP server, an mcp.json naming its Streamable HTTP endpoint,
and three skills (reader, news digest, archive research) with two reference notes. Its
server advertised eight tools. This rewrite keeps all eight -- their names, their
argument names, and their descriptions, read from the server's own tools/list -- and
posts the same JSON-RPC to the same endpoint itself through nlk:http, so no MCP client,
no Node and no local server are needed; the endpoint is stateless, so one request is
one call. The three skills' guidance (discover, then read only what the request needs;
keep every canonical link and its date; deduplicate and date-filter a digest; frame
archive research as hypotheses with counter-evidence; never pay or tip without approval
of the exact amount, asset and network, and never claim settlement without evidence) is
the cell's manual topic, (help :distro-reader), and each tool's argument list is its
declared schema. What was left out: the MCP session handshake and the untrusted-server
approval gate (the endpoint needs no session), the skills as files (they are prose, and
they are the manual), and the visual reader's payload in full -- the cell asks for link
delivery by default and clips a long page, though htmlDelivery "inline" still answers
the whole page. Nothing of the original is vendored, and no credential, key or account
is involved on either side.
